course: dictionary
lesson: 794
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so use the context to choose the right one. «A beehive on a summer day is a city of about 50,000 bees, and every bee in it has a job.» Here a beehive is the home where the bees live, not a hairstyle.
explain: Context can also show you what a word is about. «Bees can sting the soft skin inside the trunk and round the eyes.» Sting tells you that bees are dangerous, so a beehive is a place to stay calm around. Ask: which meaning fits? Then swap it into the sentence and check.
explain: Keep both meanings in mind. In «She wore her hair in a beehive for the party», the word means a hairstyle piled high on the head, because hair is being worn, not bees.
fact: A beehive is a box or other structure where bees live and make honey.
fact: A beehive is also a hairstyle piled high on the head.
fact: Inside a hive, bees have a queen, workers and drones, and they make honey in wax cells shaped like hexagons.
fact: «In Kenya, farmers hang beehives along fences, and the elephants keep away from their fields.» Elephants are wary of bees, which can sting inside the trunk.
fact: Stay calm near a beehive and move slowly. The phrase «busy as a beehive» means very busy.
exercise: «A beehive on a summer day is a city of about 50,000 bees.» What is a beehive in this sentence? | A type of flower | A busy shop in town | *A home where bees live and make honey | A hairstyle piled high on the head
exercise: «She wore her hair in a beehive for the party.» What does beehive mean here? | A garden full of flowers | *A hairstyle piled high on the head | A box where bees make honey | A tall tower in the park
exercise: Which phrase uses beehive to mean very busy? | Quiet as a mouse | Tall as a tree | *Busy as a beehive
test: Why do farmers in Kenya hang beehives on fences? | To make the fences look pretty | *To keep elephants away from their fields | To feed the elephants honey | To sell the wax to the elephants
test: What shape are the wax cells in a beehive? | A square | A triangle | A circle | *A hexagon
exam: What is the best thing to do near a beehive? | Wave your arms and run away fast | Shout loudly at the bees | *Stay calm and move slowly | Throw stones at the hive
